{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" captures state snapshots before each undoable action. Undo history lives in memory (lost on relaunch), but restored state is persisted normally via ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"restore(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you don’t use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":", nothing changes. It’s fully opt-in.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Adding Undo to Your App","level":2,"anchor":"Adding-Undo-to-Your-App","type":"heading"},{"text":"1. Create the plugin","level":3,"anchor":"1-Create-the-plugin","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass declarative predicates to classify which actions are undoable and which coalesce:"}]},{"code":["let isUndoable: @Sendable (AppAction) -> Bool = { action in","    switch action {","    case .items(.create), .items(.delete), .items(.rename): true","    case .selectItem, .toggleSidebar: false","    }","}","","let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    isUndoable: isUndoable,","    coalescing: { action in","        if case .items(.rename) = action { return true }","        return false","    }",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"2. Register and pass to Store","level":3,"anchor":"2-Register-and-pass-to-Store","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register the plugin with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"type":"text","text":" for lifecycle hooks, and pass it directly to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},{"type":"text","text":" for undo\/redo methods and "},{"code":"canUndo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"canRedo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tracking:"}]},{"code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)","","return Store(","    initialState: AppState(),","    reducer: { state, action in","        reducer.reduce(state: &state, action: action, environment: environment)","    },","    plugins: plugins,","    undoPlugin: undoPlugin,","    persistencePlugin: persistencePlugin,","    isUndoable: isUndoable",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" handles the rest internally: snapshotting state before undoable actions, restoring via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"applyRestore"},{"type":"text","text":" on undo\/redo, draining persistence changes, and updating "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canUndo"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canRedo"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"3. Wire platform UI","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"3-Wire-platform-UI"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"macOS"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — replace the Edit menu:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["WindowGroup { ... }",".commands {","    CommandGroup(replacing: .undoRedo) {","        Button(\"Undo\") { store.undo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: .command)","            .disabled(!store.canUndo)","        Button(\"Redo\") { store.redo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: [.command, .shift])","            .disabled(!store.canRedo)","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"iOS","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — bridge the system UndoManager for shake-to-undo:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ In your view — connect the environment UndoManager:",".onAppear { store.undoManager = undoManager }",".onChange(of: undoManager) { _, new in store.undoManager = new }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" automatically registers undo\/redo actions with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndoManager"},{"type":"text","text":" after each undoable dispatch."}]},{"text":"Coalescing","type":"heading","anchor":"Coalescing","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coalescing"},{"type":"text","text":" predicate groups consecutive matching actions into a single undo step. The first coalescing action captures a snapshot; subsequent consecutive coalescing actions share that snapshot. A non-coalescing action or undo\/redo resets the flag. Typing “hello” produces one undo entry, not five."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Memory","anchor":"Memory","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each snapshot is a value-type copy of your state. Cost is proportional to the number of entities across all stores. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxDepth"},{"type":"text","text":" to bound memory for large state:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(maxDepth: 50, ...)"]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"t